	Section:
		Text: References and links
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Running heads
		Paragraph: In a `Page overlay`, `{{heading 2}}` writes the last `Heading 2` that has started on the page or before it, and `{{heading 3: first}}` the first `Heading 3` that starts on the page. The header of pages 2 to 4 has both, with the number of the heading. A new chapter leaves the section empty until its first one starts.
			Style: intro
		Text: Page overlay: {{heading 2}} on the left, {{heading 3: first}} on the right
			Style: label
		Heading 2:
			Text: Installation
		Paragraph: The thermostat is installed in four steps, each one in its own section.
		Heading 3:
			Text: Before starting
		Paragraph: Switch off the power at the panel and check with a tester that the wires carry no current.
			Break:
				After: page
		Heading 3:
			Text: Wiring
		Paragraph: The red wire goes to terminal L and the blue one to terminal N. The green and yellow wire goes to the earth terminal.
		Heading 3:
			Text: Fixing
		Paragraph: The base is fixed to the wall with the two screws supplied, at a height of 1.5 meters.
			Break:
				After: page
		Heading 2:
			Text: Use
		Paragraph: This page starts a new chapter, and the right side of its header is empty until its first section starts.
			Break:
				After: page
		Heading 3:
			Text: Programs
		Paragraph: The thermostat keeps four programs for each day of the week.
